{
  "rules": [
    "Systematic Underestimation of Bullish Spikes: The model consistently fails to capture upward price surges (e.g., the rise to ~76.67), forecasting a flat or slightly declining trend while true prices spike. Correction: Apply a positive bias adjustment of +4 to +6 EUR when sentiment history shows consecutive high values (>=0.67) or when recent price momentum is strongly positive.",
    "Excessive Mean Reversion Lag: Forecasts revert to the mean too quickly after a spike, missing the sustained high plateau. Correction: Extend the duration of the elevated price level in the forecast by 3-5 days following a breakout, rather than immediately reverting to the historical average.",
    "Sentiment-Price Decoupling: High sentiment scores (1.00) are not weighted sufficiently in the model's trajectory. Correction: When sentiment is 1.00 for two consecutive days, override the model's flat/declining slope with a positive momentum slope of at least +0.5 EUR/day for the next 5 days.",
    "Overshoot in Downward Correction: After the peak, the model underestimates the speed of the subsequent decline, predicting prices that remain too high compared to the actual drop. Correction: Accelerate the downward slope in the forecast by 10-15% once the price peaks and sentiment drops below 0.5.",
    "Horizon-Specific Bias: The error is most pronounced in the first 5-10 days of the forecast horizon (the immediate future). Correction: Apply a dynamic correction factor that is strongest at day 1-5 and decays linearly to zero by day 15."
  ]
}
